00:39:08.140 --> 00:39:27.299
Daniel Glinz (Glinz & Company GmbH): So, in game theory, it's pretty simple. Just look at two parties, yourself and another party, and you're relying on this party, and you want… you have two options whether to cooperate or to defect, and also the other party has these two options. And when someone defects and the game stops, of course, you only have one iteration.

